    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for perl-File-Find-Rule.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 9.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "File::Find::Rule is a friendlier interface to File::Find.  It allows you to build rules which specify the desired files and directories.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* perl-file-find-rule: File::Find::Rule Arbitrary Code Execution (CVE-2011-10007)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
